---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { getLinks } from '../lib/links.mjs';

const count = getLinks().length;
const title = 'About akaSearch';
const description =
  'akaSearch is a community-maintained, open source directory of Microsoft aka.ms short links. It is not a Microsoft product or service.';
---

<Base title={title} description={description} canonical="/about">
  <h1 class="mt-0 text-3xl font-bold">☀️ About akaSearch</h1>

  <div class="max-w-3xl space-y-6">
    <p>
      akaSearch is a crowd-sourced directory of Microsoft's aka.ms links —
      currently {count} of them. akaSearch is not an official Microsoft product
      or service. If you like shortcuts, also check out
      <a href="https://cmd.ms" rel="noopener">cmd.ms</a>, the Microsoft Cloud
      command line.
    </p>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">🔗 What is aka.ms?</h2>
      <p>
        aka.ms is Microsoft's URL shortening service, available to Microsoft
        employees to create short links in the form
        <code>aka.ms/shortname</code>. They turn up throughout documentation,
        presentations and support articles.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">💡 Why akaSearch?</h2>
      <p>
        There are curated lists of aka.ms links, like the
        <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/dev-itpro/developer/readiness/readiness-bcall" rel="noopener">
          Dynamics 365 collection</a>, but no central place to look one up. That
        is what akaSearch is for.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">👨🏽‍🦲 Who built this?</h2>
      <p>
        This is an open source project built by
        <a href="https://merill.net" rel="noopener">Merill Fernando</a> as a
        Learning Day exercise. The source is at
        <a href="https://github.com/merill/aka" rel="noopener">github.com/merill/aka</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">✍️ How can I contribute?</h2>
      <p>
        Use the <a href="/add">Add a link</a> form — no GitHub account needed.
        To correct a title, category or destination, open a pull request against
        the <a href="https://github.com/merill/aka/tree/main/website/config" rel="noopener">config directory</a>,
        where every link is a single JSON file.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">🙅‍♂️ Is this a Microsoft product?</h2>
      <p>No. This is a community-driven project, not a Microsoft product or service.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">🤙 How can I get in touch?</h2>
      <p>
        You can reach out on
        <a href="https://twitter.com/merill" rel="noopener">Twitter</a> or
        <a href="https://github.com/merill/aka/issues" rel="noopener">open an issue on GitHub</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
